                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "058bfbed-833b-3e0a-b114-70976c98fdfc",
                        "entry_id": "e5b1b339-4440-3b96-b661-f929e23ec000",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Whatever person or persons: emphasised or elaborated form of whoever."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "formal"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1e8103e2-d8b7-41a0-bd7c-4bd83bf4dac9",
                                "sense_id": "058bfbed-833b-3e0a-b114-70976c98fdfc",
                                "text": "Whosoever partakes of this elixir shall have eternal life."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "58ce4cae-3e0b-4048-b1b1-412a823136ba",
                                "sense_id": "058bfbed-833b-3e0a-b114-70976c98fdfc",
                                "text": "If thou do pardon whoſoeuer pray, / More ſinnes for this forgiueneſs proſper may: […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4c0b9329-cf2f-444a-99b1-36fed1376454",
                                "sense_id": "058bfbed-833b-3e0a-b114-70976c98fdfc",
                                "text": "Whoſoeuer commeth to me, and heareth my ſayings, and doeth them, I will ſhew you to whom he is like."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9f0f6fa0-ef66-4152-8802-44cb8670437e",
                                "sense_id": "058bfbed-833b-3e0a-b114-70976c98fdfc",
                                "text": "His mercy is a panacea, a balſome for an afflicted ſoule, a Soveraigne medicine, an alexipharmacum for all ſinne, a charme for the Divell, his mercy was great to Solomon, to Manaſſes, to Peter, great to all offenders, and whoſoever thou art, it may be ſo to thee."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "064ca38e-48eb-49c2-957d-0ecb40ee8028",
                                "sense_id": "058bfbed-833b-3e0a-b114-70976c98fdfc",
                                "text": "This world, after all our science and sciences, is still a miracle; wonderful, inscrutable, magical and more, to whosoever will think of it."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f7473ecc-9bec-4c01-aecd-8ac2d5fdb53a",
                                "sense_id": "058bfbed-833b-3e0a-b114-70976c98fdfc",
                                "text": "Whosoever shall be found without the soul for getting down, must stand and face the hounds of hell"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
        ],
